WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.740
Old Nan: I could tell you about Ser Duncan
the Tall, those were always your favorites.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:07.740
George R.R.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:13.460
Martin: I have to do this, I have to do a
prequel.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.860
So I started thinking about my history and
what would be a good area to write it and

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.860
I came up with the Dunk and Egg stuff.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.910
I was particularly attracted that whole story
is built around a tournament and I love medieval

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.460
tournaments, reading about them, writing about
them.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:33.770
There are, of course, some of them in the
main books but this was an opportunity in

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:38.870
a time of peace, not war, to look at a medieval
tilt tournament with all its pageantryand

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:41.430
the jousting and the combat.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.700
And reveal little of Westerosi history.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.820
Joffrey Baratheon: So this is the famous Book
of Brothers.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.890
All the great deeds of all the great Kingsguard,
huh?

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:53.820
Ser Duncan the Tall.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.270
Hah, four pages for Ser Duncan.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:01:02.449
Must have been quite a man.

00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:15.330
Jaime Lannister: So they say.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.950
All boys dream of becoming knights.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:21.439
The boys with talent dream of becoming Kingsguard.

00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:24.750
The boys without talent, well, I wouldn't
know.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.810
For centuries, the Kingsguard have been the
glory of the realm.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:33.460
Aegon the Conqueror had established the order
as his personal guardians after uniting Westeros

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.250
with fire and blood.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:39.450
He knew that some of his subjects wouldn't
take to conquest, and his dragons were no

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.880
use against knives in the dark.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.570
No doubt surrounding himself with the greatest
knights in Westeros made his rule more palatable

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:49.230
and less foreign as well.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:53.649
Everyone in his kingdoms soon knew the names
and some of the songs of the Kingsguard.

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:55.720
I certainly did from earliest days.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.299
We protected the king and his family.

00:01:58.299 --> 00:02:00.750
We killed his enemies and led his armies.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:04.590
We gave him counsel when asked and kept his
secrets when not.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:08.080
We swore to hold no lands, take no wives,
and father no children.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.730
Like the Night's Watch, except with a real
job to do.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:17.730
Was I awed to see my name inscribed in the
same book as my heroes?

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.230
Of course not.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:20.879
I was sixteen and brilliant.

00:02:20.879 --> 00:02:23.640
I knew I belonged there.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.720
Beside the name of Ser Duncan the Tall, who,
as a hedge knight, broke several of Prince

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.030
Aerion Targaryen's teeth while defending a
Dornish woman.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:36.000
He later rose to Lord Commander and burned
beside his King at Summerhall, because Ser

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.379
Duncan had sworn our oath.

00:02:38.379 --> 00:02:40.360
Bronn: Justice is a funny thing.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:45.380
For the poor, it's what keeps them alive - and
starving; Depending on how the local lord

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:48.739
feels about his woods, his streams, his crops.

00:02:48.739 --> 00:02:54.180
For the rich, justice is what you get if you
are not careful enough - or rich enough.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:58.569
Usually how it works is: you commit a crime
and the local lord sends his guards after

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:02.640
you; or your victim's family kills you and
the guards go after them instead.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.230
Or you do nothing, and the guards come after
you anyway.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:09.630
Either way, someone is brought before the
lord and he decides what's to be done.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.500
Could be a fine, if you are rich enough to
pay.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.450
Otherwise it's the dungeons, the chopping
block or the Wall.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:19.549
If your family honor goes back hundreds of
years to a time when your ancestors hit other

00:03:19.549 --> 00:03:24.470
men harder than they were hit, you had another
option: trial by combat.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.741
You either fight your accuser, or you both
pick champions to fight on your behalf, and

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:33.930
the gods will favor the righteous man... as
long as he's also the strongest, the quickest

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.160
or the luckiest.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:40.090
Once in a long while, you may get two real
highborn shits having a go at each other;

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:44.519
and one of them might be fool enough to demand
a trial by seven.

00:03:44.519 --> 00:03:47.400
Exactly how it sounds: seven men against seven
men.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.459
Makes for a good show,I guess.

00:03:49.459 --> 00:03:53.860
But any man who's been in battle knows that
the more men involved, the less skill needed,

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:56.019
the more chance of accidents.

00:03:56.019 --> 00:04:00.060
Just ask that Targaryen prince who got his
head staved in by his brother all those years

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.060
ago.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:02.549
And all for some hedge knight.

00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:07.879
Varys: A wheel with two hubs will not turn,
and a kingdom with two kings will burn, as

00:04:07.879 --> 00:04:09.420
the saying goes.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:15.019
Not that such a cost stopped anyone with even
the remotest claim and opportunity, much less

00:04:15.019 --> 00:04:17.549
House Blackfyre.

00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:22.250
Their rebellions consumed tens of years and
thousands of lives.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:28.760
First Daemon's own, then his son, Daemon the
Second, who reigned for a night.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:34.760
Then another son, Haegon, crowned by Bittersteel,
another legitimized bastard who had founded

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:38.419
the Golden Company to support the Blackfyre
claim.

00:04:38.419 --> 00:04:44.539
When Haegon was executed, Bittersteel crowned
Haegon's elder son Daemon the Third, who,

00:04:44.539 --> 00:04:49.400
in turn, was slain by the Lord Commander of
the Kingsguard, Ser Duncan the Tall.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:53.430
Ray: "The War of the NinepennyKings", they
called it.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:57.540
But I never saw a king or earned a penny.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:02.139
After the war ended, I heard it all started
when an exiled royal bastard raised an army

00:05:02.139 --> 00:05:07.790
of sellswords and the rightful king sent his
own army to stop an invasion.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:10.220
Sounds simple, the way the Maesters tell it.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:13.490
But an army isn't like a dog that comes when
you whistle.

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:18.919
The king calls on great lords, who call on
lesser lords, who send down their captains

00:05:18.919 --> 00:05:22.710
to round up all the peasant men on the land
the lord claims to own.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:27.870
If the lord is wise and generous, his new
soldiers are given steel swords and wooden

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.090
shields to fight his battles.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:33.660
Most of our army fought with sharp sticks.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:37.020
Singers still sing of the valiant heroes made
in the war.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.070
Ser Brynden Tully, the "Blackfish."

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:46.630
Ser Tywin Lannister and Prince Aerys Targaryen.Ser
Barristan Selmy, the "Bold," who slew the

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:50.090
bastard pretender and ended the war at a stroke.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:52.910
But the king whose crown we were defending
never came.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:55.440
He mattered too much, I suppose.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:06:00.040
His Hand commanded the crown's armies and
died valiantly in his son's arms.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.970
Or so the singers say.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:04.819
I never saw that, either.

00:06:04.819 --> 00:06:07.919
I did see the soldiers when they came to our
village.

00:06:07.919 --> 00:06:11.729
They declared I was too young to fight but
my brothers and friends were all going and

00:06:11.729 --> 00:06:13.610
I wouldn't be left behind.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:18.620
My oldest brother said I could be his squire,
though he wasn't a knight, just a pot boy

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:21.100
armed with a stolen kitchen knife.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.470
He'd never need it.

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:26.450
I saw him collapse on our march from fever,
along with many from our village.

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:31.849
I saw our shoes fall apart on the road, our
clothes rot off our bodies and half of us

00:06:31.849 --> 00:06:34.050
shitting our beds from the sickness and fear.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:36.539
And then we got to the war.

00:06:36.539 --> 00:06:42.060
In the Stepstones, I saw a mace cave in my
last brother's head, I saw the lord who led

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:45.910
us there cut down, and some other lord shout
that we were his now.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:49.199
One day I looked around and realized all my
friends and kin were gone.

00:06:49.199 --> 00:06:53.070
I was fighting beside strangers under a banner
I'd never seen.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.520
Didn't know where I was or how to get home.

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:00.570
When a lord ran up shouting at us to form
ranks with our scythes and hoes, I couldn't

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:02.190
remember which side I was on.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:06.720
Then the knights came down on us, faceless
men all in steel.

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:09.970
The thunder of their charge filled the world.

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:12.819
I closed my eyes.

00:07:12.819 --> 00:07:19.860
Years later, after the war had faded into
songs, I opened them again and saw what I

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:26.360
had done and what I had become in the war
and since.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.230
I went looking for a way back home.

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:34.000
I know I'll never reach it, but that doesn't
mean I don't need a guide.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.660
Samwell Tarly: According to legend, House
Targaryen survived the Doom of Valyria thanks

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:44.280
to Daenys the Dreamer, who foresaw the calamity
and convinced her father to flee their homeland.

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:46.449
It could be true.

00:07:46.449 --> 00:07:49.370
The Targaryens were always a bit more.

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:54.310
But as Maester Yandel points out, in the East,
the Targaryens were one of a thousand minor

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:58.360
noble families, and in Westeros, they became
kings.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:03.720
Politics, not prophecy, could have drawn them
to our shores.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:09.610
Politics can also explain the prophecies of
Daemon II Blackfyre, a Targaryen bastard rumored

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:12.250
to possess the family gift.

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:16.190
While posing as a hedge knight, he told a
future Lord Commander of the Kingsguard that

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:20.830
he dreamt of a dragon hatching at Whitewalls
Castle and took it as a sign that he'd win

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.800
the Iron Throne.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:26.539
Perhaps if he'd slept a bit longer, he'd have
dreamt of the King's Hand putting down his

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:30.539
rebellion a day later, before it even began.

00:08:30.539 --> 00:08:36.149
Most Maesters dismiss all Targaryen claims
of prophecy as mystic nonsense, a relic of

00:08:36.149 --> 00:08:38.789
their Eastern ancestry.

00:08:38.789 --> 00:08:43.740
To be fair, across the Narrow Sea, there isn't
a market without a Warlock from Qarth telling

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.200
fortunes or a shadowbinder from Asshai reading
fates in blood.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:52.940
Or so I hear from the Maesters.

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:58.510
Pycelle: the Targaryens never stopped trying
to revive their dragons.

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:03.480
AerionBrightflame drank a draught of wildfire
and burned to death.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:10.839
Aegon the Fifth tried to hatch stone dragon
eggs with sorcery and burned to death.

00:09:10.839 --> 00:09:16.970
Jon Snow: Sam said you wanted to see me.

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:17.970
Aemon Targaryen: I did, indeed.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:19.680
Jon Snow: Who are you?

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:27.810
Aemon Targaryen: My father was Maekar, the
First of his Name.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:37.190
My brother Aegon reigned after him, when I
had refused the throne.

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:41.170
Robb Stark: What are you telling him now?

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:51.730
Old Nan: Only what the little Lord wants to
hear.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:10:03.360
Robb Stark: Get your supper, I want some time
with him.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:09.700
Aemon Targaryen: Mother’s looking for you…

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:10.750
Egg.

